preConditionHook:
// THE RESTING LIMIT ORDER AT A MULTIPLE OF INITIAL RISK. A long is closed when
// the bar's own high reaches EntryPrice + riskMultiple * stopDistance; the
// short mirrors on the bar's low. Six Grimes restatements of one target
// (G06-10, G06-19, G06-59, G08-05, G08-06, G10-01); book values 1 and 2 are a
// GRID RANGE, not two rules.
//
// THE ENGINE HAS NO INITIAL-RISK ACCESSOR, so the risk unit is a stopDistance
// INPUT IN PRICE POINTS (merge decision 24, the RewardRiskDeteriorationExit
// spelling). Keeping it equal to the stop placement's own distance is the
// placement author's job; nothing enforces it.
//
// PARTIAL PROFITS ARE NOT EXPRESSIBLE: each risk multiple is a FULL exit
// placement (decision 24), and Grimes's 25-50 percent / "more than half"
// fractions are recorded, not mechanized.
//
// NOT TakeProfit, which fires on ctx.OpenPositionProfit() -- the close-marked
// dollar mark net of the entry side's costs. This fires on the bar's own
// extreme, the limit fill Grimes describes, and carries no stop leg. Not
// CountertrendScalpAtrTarget either: that sizes the target in ATRs frozen at
// entry and tests the close.
//
// The MarketPosition guard is load-bearing: ctx.EntryPrice() is 0.0 while flat
// and a back-adjusted series carries an arbitrary offset.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 0.
